WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:12.120
[Music]

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.500
I'm really excited

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:20.540
We're here in Moscow in Russia in the Central House of Scientists of the Russian Academy of Sciences...

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.100
...for the ceremony for the naming of 3 of the elements

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.060
115, 117, 118

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.400
And, I've got to make a speech...

00:00:30.455 --> 00:00:32.995
...in Russian. I'm a bit nervous

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.960
But, I hope it'll be alright

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:43.900
[Music]

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:38.680
This element is unique in the periodic table because...

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.040
...it's never been observed in any form at all

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.720
So, the field's wide open

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.860
[Music]

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.960
This is, after all, what's Mendeleev's triumph for the periodic table was...

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.640
...that he looked where there were holes in the periodic table... where he reckoned there should be elements...

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.500
...and he predicted their properties

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.440
[Music]

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:08.000
If you're really lucky, little bits fall off ... particles...one particle after another

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.260
[Music]

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.600
I believe that somebody will make element 118 quite soon

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.500
Some folk in Russia in Dubna ...

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.620
I missed a really exciting piece of news...

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.200
... had managed to...to make a new element!

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.800
...the most exciting piece of the news about the periodic table ...

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.620
...that's happened since we've started these videos

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.800
So this is the periodic table as we know it

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.300
They haven't actually officially approved the names yet

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.200
But they've said these are the names that we're considering

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:44.320
If a beam is directed into the centre of the target

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.780
[Music]

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.760
It's almost like a chill goes up your spine...

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.700
...it's like, "Wow, something new, something really exciting!"

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.000
And now I will show you how it looks like and I will open the box

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.685
I'm very excited. Never seen anything like this before

00:03:01.805 --> 00:03:03.800
So it's really ... a real first for me

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.600
I've never met anybody who's discovered an element

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.955
And you go on throwing and throwing...

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.700
...more and more

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:16.740
So now's the time to put in your bid for the name for element 117

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.300
I met a representative of Riken

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.820
Nihonium, Moscovium, Tennessine and Oganesson

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.440
But certainly people get very passionate about names

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.760
So, one name is Russian and the other name is American

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.800
Now the important question that people always ask is ...

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.200
...what on earth is the point of making elements like this?

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.205
We've even produced a little radioactive liquid sample

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.360
It is testing theories and things like that that really move science forward

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.540
[Music]

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.960
Three atoms...

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.900
...of this element

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.100
[Music]

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.260
Afterwards there was cake and champagne and it was really good

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.340
[Music]

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:09.240
He is a pioneer and very long time researcher in Dubna

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.840
It's extremely unlikely that this will happen again...

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.400
...four elements at once...

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.640
...for a very long time, if ever

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.620
It's almost akin to the announcement of the Nobel prizes...

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.000
...and celebration of good science

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.860
So yeah, it's a really exciting time

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:37.680
[Music]

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.080
[Applause]

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.460
[Music]

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:25.300
[Applause]

